RozeLynx netiface v14: session-restore hook — re-apply the per-tab interface
binding from the SessionStore custom tab value ("rozelynxNetIface") in the
parent process, synchronously, inside restoreTab().

Why: the tab-layer binding is keyed by BrowsingContext::BrowserId() in the
netiface component's runtime map, and every restored tab (undo-close via
Ctrl+Shift+T / Recently Closed Tabs, startup session restore, closed-window
restore) gets a FRESH BrowserId.  The RozeLynx Features extension re-applies
the binding when it observes the new tab (tabs.onCreated/tabs.onUpdated), but
as an MV3 event page it is typically suspended and wakes a beat too late:
the restored document's history restore (queued at the end of restoreTab)
opens its first TCP connections on the profile-default interface before the
rebind lands, so a reopen-closed-tab visibly "reopens in the profile
default".  Doing it here — before _sendRestoreHistory()/TabRestoreQueue run
— beats the page load by construction; the extension's rebind becomes a
benign no-op (its getEffective() equality check).

The binding itself is written by the extension through
SessionStore.setCustomTabValue(...) as JSON.stringify(String(iface)) and
survives close/reopen through the closed-tab entry's extData (weakmap
collect at onTabClose, TAB_CUSTOM_VALUES restore here).

Best effort, version-agnostic (context anchors identical in 154-156):
builds without the @bytewheel.org/netiface;1 component (USE=-net-iface)
throw on the getService and skip through the catch; malformed/missing
values are ignored.  Chrome globals Cc/Ci are already used by this module.

--- a/browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs
+++ b/browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs
@@ -6560,6 +6560,27 @@
       TAB_CUSTOM_VALUES.delete(tab);
     }
 
+    // RozeLynx netiface: apply a persisted per-tab interface binding to the
+    // fresh BrowserId BEFORE the content restore below can open the tab's
+    // first TCP connection (see patch header).  Best effort: no netiface
+    // component, no BrowserId or no persisted value => skip silently.
+    try {
+      const rozelynxRaw = tabData.extData && tabData.extData.rozelynxNetIface;
+      if (typeof rozelynxRaw == "string" && rozelynxRaw) {
+        const rozelynxIface = JSON.parse(rozelynxRaw);
+        if (typeof rozelynxIface == "string" && rozelynxIface) {
+          const bc = browser.browsingContext;
+          const top = bc ? (bc.top || bc) : null;
+          if (top && top.browserId) {
+            const svc = Cc["@bytewheel.org/netiface;1"].getService(
+              Ci.nsIRozeLynxNetIface
+            );
+            svc.setTabInterface(top.browserId, rozelynxIface);
+          }
+        }
+      }
+    } catch (e) {}
+
     // Tab is now open.
     delete tabData.closedAt;
 
